PatchClosure-Bench repro — openstack-glance-cve-2015-1195
Pair: CVE-2014-9493 (OSSA-2014-041)  ->  CVE-2015-1195 (OSSA-2015-002)
Root cause: arbitrary host-file disclosure via Glance v2 image-location scheme (CWE-22)
Gate variant: A (same sink/channel: image-location -> filesystem store read)

VERSIONS (real openstack/glance, exact commits; store_utils.py fetched at build)
  V0  81b3c04eca4378d9f2c0f63c8692276cbc1cf5b3  parent of the 9493 fix (no guard)
  V1  4afdb017aa1ccef01482f117cb8d0736a6da38ed  CVE-2014-9493 fix (TARGET)   "To prevent client use v2 patch api to handle file and swift location"
  V2  a2d986b976e9325a272e2d422465165315d19fe6  CVE-2015-1195 fix            "Prevent file, swift+config and filesystem schemes"

MECHANISM (incomplete fix)
  CVE-2014-9493 added glance/common/store_utils.py::validate_external_location():
      valid_schemes = [s for s in store_api.get_known_schemes()
                       if s != 'file' and s != 'swift+config']
      return urlparse(uri).scheme in valid_schemes
  The glance_store filesystem backend registers BOTH 'file' AND 'filesystem'
  schemes for the same local-file store (get_known_schemes() ->
  ['file','filesystem','http','https']). The blocklist dropped only 'file', so
  'filesystem:///<abs path>' still passes the guard and the filesystem store
  reads the host file = CVE-2015-1195. V2 adds
  RESTRICTED_URI_SCHEMAS = frozenset(['file','filesystem','swift+config']).

HARNESS (faithful, no glance code edited)
  Each container runs the REAL store_utils.py at its commit (guard-irrelevant
  sibling imports stubbed; the guard is a pure fn of urlparse().scheme +
  glance_store.get_known_schemes()). glance_store==2.0.1 is the genuine library;
  its filesystem backend performs the REAL read-exfil (get_from_backend) of an
  absolute path outside filesystem_store_datadir (=/var/lib/glance/images).
  Canary: entrypoint writes ${PCB_FLAG} to /canary/secret.txt (outside datadir).
  Probe: GET /read?scheme=<file|filesystem>&path=/canary/secret.txt.

